{%- comment -%}
  fye-hero — the pattern every content section follows. Read this before
  writing another one. 68 uses, the most of any section.

  THE CONTRACT:
    - Root element is `.band band--{colour}` + an inner `.wrap`.
    - The `band` setting picks the ground. That is the ONLY thing controlling
      background colour, and --sect-y is the ONLY thing controlling padding.
    - This section declares NO padding, NO colours, NO breakpoints.
      Everything comes from fye-core.css.
    - Section CSS below is scoped `.fye .hero`, never a bare `.hero`.

  Setting IDs are frozen to match the old theme so existing JSON templates
  keep working. Do not rename them.

  ADDED 27/08/2026, so the homepage hero can be built without raw HTML
  The live homepage hero was six blocks of hand-written HTML in text settings —
  an <h1> with fourteen inline styles, two <a> tags with their own colours and
  hover states, and two spacer blocks whose only job was margin. All of it is
  now settings:
    - `align` — the CSS for a left-aligned hero already existed with no way to
      reach it.
    - `logo_url`, `logo_alt`, `logo_width` — a wordmark above the heading. A
      text URL rather than an image picker because the live value is a Files
      URL, not a shop_images reference.
    - `link_label`, `link_url` — the quiet underlined link under the buttons
      ("Or book a free London or online consultation").
    - `heading_style` — see below.

  DEVIATION FROM THE BRAND BOOK, and why
  The brand book says H1 is Tenor Sans UPPERCASE. That is right for two or
  three words ("Timeless Engagement Rings") and wrong for the homepage's h1,
  which is a full sentence of 100 characters. Set in uppercase at the H1 scale
  it is both unreadable and shouty — the live site already renders it sentence
  case at a smaller size, which was the correct instinct. So `heading_style`
  offers:
    display  — uppercase, tracked, full H1 scale. The brand default.
    sentence — sentence case, one step down the scale, tracking relaxed.
  Use `sentence` only for a heading that is genuinely a sentence.

  ADDED 26/09/2026 (Route 1 homepage, Claude Design canvas "FYE Hero
  Sections", option A). Both additions are opt-in, so the other heroes that
  use this section render exactly as before:
    - `copy_position` — `bottom` drops the copy to the foot of a taller
      photograph instead of centring it. Only takes effect with an image.
    - `category` blocks — a row of shop-by-category links along the foot of
      the hero, under a hairline, each with an optional small badge ("New").
      With no blocks nothing is rendered. On a narrow screen the row scrolls
      sideways rather than wrapping; it is one set of markup at every width.
      A block for a collection that does not exist yet should be hidden in
      the editor (it is saved as "disabled") until the collection is live.
  `logo_words_position: start` no longer needs a wordmark image. The homepage
  dropped the image (the header already carries the logo) but keeps the
  brand words at the start of the h1 for W406.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings
  assign band = s.band | default: 'ivory'
  assign align = s.align | default: 'center'
  assign hstyle = s.heading_style | default: 'display'
  assign hero_alt = s.heading | default: shop.name | strip_html
  assign has_img = false
  if s.image != blank
    assign has_img = true
  endif

  comment
    The wordmark completes the heading ("Engagement rings by" + [FOR YOUR
    ETERNITY]), so to a crawler or a screen reader the <h1> alone was a
    fragment (audit 02/09/2026, P1). When a wordmark follows, its words go
    INSIDE the h1 as visually-hidden text and the image becomes decorative,
    so the sentence is read once and looks exactly as before.
  endcomment
  assign logo_words = s.logo_alt | default: shop.name | strip_html

  comment
    25/09/2026 (W406): `logo_words_first` moves those hidden words to the
    START of the h1, with no visual change. Google auto-corrects "for your
    eternity" to the anime To Your Eternity, and the homepage h1 was 15
    words of tagline with the brand as its last word. The h1 is one of the
    strongest signals Google uses to decide what a site is called, so on
    the homepage it now reads "For Your Eternity: Beautifully made...".
    The landing pages keep the default, where the heading is written to
    run into the wordmark ("Wedding rings by" [FOR YOUR ETERNITY]).
  endcomment
  assign logo_words_first = false
  if s.logo_words_position == 'start'
    assign logo_words_first = true
  endif

  assign pos_class = ''
  if has_img and s.copy_position == 'bottom'
    assign pos_class = ' hero--bottom'
  endif
  assign cat_blocks = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'category'
-%}

<div class="band band--{{ band }} hero hero--{{ align }}{% if has_img %} hero--media{% endif %}{{ pos_class }}" data-screen-label="Hero">
  {%- if has_img -%}
    <div class="hero__media scrim">
      {%- comment -%}
        fetchpriority="high": this photograph is the LCP element on the
        homepage and the three landing pages, and without the hint it queued
        behind the header logos and the first product images (audit S4).
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {{ s.image | image_url: width: 2400 | image_tag:
         alt: hero_alt,
         class: 'hero__img',
         loading: 'eager',
         fetchpriority: 'high',
         sizes: '100vw',
         widths: '600,900,1200,1600,2000,2400' }}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="wrap hero__in">
    {%- if s.eyebrow != blank -%}
      <p class="eyebrow">{{ s.eyebrow }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if s.heading != blank -%}
      {%- if logo_words_first -%}
        <h1 class="hero__title hero__title--{{ hstyle }}"><span class="visually-hidden">{{ logo_words }}: </span>{{ s.heading }}</h1>
      {%- else -%}
        <h1 class="hero__title hero__title--{{ hstyle }}">{{ s.heading }}{% if s.logo_url != blank %} <span class="visually-hidden">{{ logo_words }}</span>{% endif %}</h1>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      The wordmark sits BELOW the heading, because the heading is written to
      run into it — "Wedding Rings by" / [FOR YOUR ETERNITY]. Above the
      heading it reads as a stray mark and the sentence dangles.

      alt="" and aria-hidden: the words are already in the h1 above. When
      there is no heading the image carries the name itself.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if s.logo_url != blank -%}
      {%- if s.heading != blank -%}
        <img class="hero__logo" src="{{ s.logo_url }}" alt="" aria-hidden="true"
          style="--logo-w: {{ s.logo_width | default: 250 }}px;" loading="eager">
      {%- else -%}
        <img class="hero__logo" src="{{ s.logo_url }}" alt="{{ logo_words | escape }}"
          style="--logo-w: {{ s.logo_width | default: 250 }}px;" loading="eager">
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if s.subheading != blank -%}
      <p class="lead hero__sub">{{ s.subheading }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if s.button_label != blank -%}
      <div class="row hero__actions">
        <a class="btn" href="{{ s.button_link | default: '#' }}">{{ s.button_label }}</a>
        {%- if s.button2_label != blank -%}
          <a class="btn btn--outline" href="{{ s.button2_link | default: '#' }}">{{ s.button2_label }}</a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if s.link_label != blank -%}
      <a class="hero__link" href="{{ s.link_url | default: '#' }}">{{ s.link_label }}</a>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- if cat_blocks.size > 0 -%}
    <nav class="wrap hero__cats" aria-label="{{ s.cats_label | default: 'Shop by category' | escape }}">
      {%- for block in cat_blocks -%}
        {%- assign b = block.settings -%}
        {%- if b.label != blank -%}
          <a class="hero__cat" href="{{ b.link | default: '#' }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
            {{- b.label -}}
            {%- if b.badge != blank %}<span class="hero__cat-badge">{{ b.badge }}</span>{% endif -%}
          </a>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </nav>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
.fye .hero__in {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--s5);
  text-align: center;
}
/* Left-aligned heroes run wide: on a full-bleed photograph the centred 1320px
   measure left a 124px gap before the copy at laptop width, which reads as a
   mistake rather than a margin. Live uses 1368 plus the gutter. */
.fye .hero--left .hero__in {
  align-items: flex-start;
  text-align: left;
  max-width: var(--maxw-wide);
  /* Twice live's 24px gutter. The left-aligned hero is the only place the
     copy has a real left edge against a full-bleed photograph, and at one
     gutter it sat too close to it. */
  padding-inline-start: 48px;
}
@media (max-width: 560px) {
  /* 48px of a 375px screen is a seventh of the width. Back to the gutter. */
  .fye .hero--left .hero__in { padding-inline-start: var(--gutter, 16px); }
}

/* Tightened against the heading it completes, not floated in the stack. */
.fye .hero__logo { width: var(--logo-w, 250px); height: auto; margin-top: calc(var(--s5) * -0.5); }
.fye .hero__sub { max-width: 56ch; }
.fye .hero__actions { justify-content: center; margin-top: var(--s3); }
.fye .hero--left .hero__actions { justify-content: flex-start; }

/* Brand default: uppercase, tracked, short. */
.fye .hero__title--display { max-width: 24ch; }

/* A heading that is a sentence. One step down the scale, no uppercase, and a
   wider measure because sentences need line length. See the note above. */
.fye .hero__title--sentence {
  font-size: var(--fs-h2);
  letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  text-transform: none;
  max-width: 34ch;
}

/* The quiet secondary link. Underlined rather than a third button, so it does
   not compete with the two that matter. */
.fye .hero__link {
  font-size: var(--fs-small);
  text-decoration: underline;
  text-underline-offset: 4px;
}

/* With a photograph: the band becomes the frame, the image fills it, and type
   sits on the brand's teal scrim. Padding still comes from --sect-y. */
.fye .hero--media { position: relative; overflow: hidden; }
/* 42% is tuned for a mid-tone photograph. The homepage hero is pale skin and a
   white ring, where ivory type at 42% is not readable — 55%, measured against
   the lightest area of that image. */
.fye .hero--media .hero__media { position: absolute; inset: 0; --scrim: rgba(35, 61, 71, 0.55); }
.fye .hero--media .hero__img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }
/* width: 100% is load-bearing. .hero--media is display:flex, which makes this
   wrap a flex item — without an explicit width it shrink-to-fits its own text
   and .wrap's auto margins then centre that narrow box, indenting the copy by
   a few hundred px. See the ninth non-negotiable in conventions.md. */
.fye .hero--media .hero__in { position: relative; z-index: 1; width: 100%; }
.fye .hero--media .hero__in,
.fye .hero--media :where(h1, .eyebrow, .lead),
.fye .hero--media .hero__link { color: var(--on-dark); }
.fye .hero--media .btn { background: var(--ivory); border-color: var(--ivory); color: var(--teal); }
.fye .hero--media .btn:hover { background: var(--sage); border-color: var(--sage); color: var(--teal); }
.fye .hero--media .btn--outline { background: transparent; border-color: var(--ivory); color: var(--ivory); }
.fye .hero--media .btn--outline:hover { background: var(--ivory); color: var(--teal); }

/* A hero with a photograph needs height even when the copy is short. Not a
   setting: the old section had three (580/460/390) and they were the same
   proportion at every width. */
.fye .hero--media { min-height: 580px; display: flex; align-items: center; }
@media (max-width: 900px) { .fye .hero--media { min-height: 460px; } }
@media (max-width: 560px) { .fye .hero--media { min-height: 390px; } }

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   TOUCH TARGETS, 03/09/2026. Found by fyeSmoke on the live homepage at 889px.
   .hero__link measured 294x24 against the 44px minimum (conventions §7).
   inline-flex because min-height does nothing to an inline box, and padding
   would push the link off the hero copy baseline.
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
.fye .hero__link {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  min-height: 44px;
}

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   COPY AT THE FOOT, 26/09/2026. Route 1 homepage: a tall photograph with the
   copy sitting low on it, the way the Claude Design canvas drew it. Heights
   are measured from that canvas (800 desktop, a full phone screen on mobile)
   and trimmed for the header above; literals, like the three above, because
   they belong to this one layout.
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
.fye .hero--bottom {
  flex-direction: column;
  justify-content: flex-end;
  align-items: stretch;
  gap: var(--s9);
  min-height: 720px;
}
/* The one vertical padding rule in this file, deliberately (26/09/2026, Ed:
   "the spacing vertically is slightly off"). The category row is the foot of
   the hero, so the band's bottom --sect-y left it floating 80px above the
   edge with dead photograph under it. Same device as the band-after-band
   reset in fye-core.css; the row supplies its own breathing room below. */
.fye .hero--bottom:has(.hero__cats) { padding-block-end: 0; }
@media (max-width: 900px) { .fye .hero--bottom { min-height: 620px; } }
@media (max-width: 560px) { .fye .hero--bottom { min-height: 600px; gap: var(--s7); } }

/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   SHOP-BY-CATEGORY ROW. Hairline above, labels in the eyebrow voice at the
   fine size so seven of them fit the 1320 measure. Spread across the width
   when there is room; scrolls sideways when there is not (never wraps, so
   the row stays one line on a phone). Colour follows the ground: ivory on a
   photograph or a teal band, ink elsewhere.
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
.fye .hero__cats {
  position: relative;
  z-index: 1;
  width: 100%;
  display: flex;
  /* Packed from the left with a fixed gap, not spread: with three links,
     space-between threw them to the far corners and the row stopped reading
     as a row. Seven fit the measure at this gap. */
  justify-content: flex-start;
  gap: var(--s10);
  border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  padding-block: var(--s5) var(--s7);
  overflow-x: auto;
  scrollbar-width: none;
}
.fye .hero__cats::-webkit-scrollbar { display: none; }
/* Width, not padding, so the hairline starts where the copy starts: the copy
   is inset 48px inside a --maxw-wide wrap (see .hero--left .hero__in). */
.fye .hero--left .hero__cats { width: calc(100% - 96px); max-width: calc(var(--maxw-wide) - 96px); }
@media (max-width: 560px) {
  .fye .hero--left .hero__cats { width: calc(100% - 2 * var(--gutter, 16px)); }
  .fye .hero__cats { gap: var(--s7); padding-block-end: var(--s5); }
}
.fye .hero--media .hero__cats { border-top-color: var(--line-on-dark); }
.fye .hero__cat {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--s2);
  min-height: 44px;
  flex-shrink: 0;
  white-space: nowrap;
  font-size: var(--fs-fine);
  font-weight: var(--fw-medium);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-eyebrow);
  text-transform: uppercase;
  text-decoration: none;
  color: inherit;
}
.fye .hero--media .hero__cat { color: var(--on-dark); }
.fye .hero__cat:hover { color: var(--sage); }
.fye .hero--media .hero__cat:hover { color: var(--sage-grey); }
/* Teal on sage-grey: 7.0:1, computed in sRGB (#233D47 on #C8CDC7). */
.fye .hero__cat-badge {
  font-size: var(--fs-eyebrow);
  letter-spacing: var(--tr-eyebrow);
  line-height: 1;
  padding: 3px 6px;
  background: var(--sage-grey);
  color: var(--teal);
}
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Hero",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Timeless engagement rings" },
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "heading_style", "label": "Heading style", "default": "display",
      "info": "Sentence case for a heading that is a full sentence — uppercase is for two or three words.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "display",  "label": "Uppercase display" },
        { "value": "sentence", "label": "Sentence case" }
      ]
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "subheading", "label": "Subheading" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Background image", "info": "Optional. Type sits on a teal scrim when set." },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Logo" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "logo_url", "label": "Logo URL", "info": "A file URL. Shown above the heading." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "logo_alt", "label": "Logo description" },
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "logo_words_position", "label": "Logo words in the heading", "default": "end",
      "info": "Where the logo description is read in the heading by search engines and screen readers. Looks the same either way.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "end",   "label": "After the heading" },
        { "value": "start", "label": "Before the heading" }
      ]
    },
    { "type": "range", "id": "logo_width", "label": "Logo width", "default": 250, "min": 100, "max": 400, "step": 10, "unit": "px" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Buttons" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "button_label", "label": "Button label" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "button_link", "label": "Button link" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "button2_label", "label": "Second button label" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "button2_link", "label": "Second button link" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "link_label", "label": "Text link", "info": "A quieter third option, under the buttons." },
    { "type": "url", "id": "link_url", "label": "Text link URL" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Layout" },
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "copy_position", "label": "Copy position", "default": "middle",
      "info": "With a background image only. Bottom makes the hero taller and sits the copy low on the photograph.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "middle", "label": "Middle" },
        { "value": "bottom", "label": "Bottom" }
      ]
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cats_label", "label": "Category links name", "default": "Shop by category", "info": "Read by screen readers. Only used when there are category link blocks." },
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "align", "label": "Alignment", "default": "center",
      "options": [
        { "value": "center", "label": "Centred" },
        { "value": "left",   "label": "Left" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "band",
      "label": "Background band",
      "info": "Padding and type colour follow automatically.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "white", "label": "White" },
        { "value": "ivory", "label": "Champagne ivory" },
        { "value": "mist", "label": "Mist blue" },
        { "value": "teal", "label": "Eternal teal" },
        { "value": "sage", "label": "Sage green" }
      ],
      "default": "ivory"
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "category",
      "name": "Category link",
      "limit": 10,
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "label", "label": "Label" },
        { "type": "url", "id": "link", "label": "Link" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "badge", "label": "Badge", "info": "Optional, e.g. New." }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    { "name": "Hero" }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}

